{"seq":26,"slug":"ruby-language","title":"Ruby 语言","stage":"DONE","category":"languages","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/ruby-language","rating":{"composite":3.61,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.8,"coverage":3,"positioning":null,"strategic":4},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"introMarkdown":"# Ruby 语言\n\n1995 年圣诞节，松本行弘把第一版 Ruby 公开发布；三十年后的 2025 年圣诞节，Ruby 4.0 如约而至。这门语言始终被同一句话定义：让程序员快乐。它不是为机器写得最快而生，而是为读代码、改代码的人写得最顺手而生。理解 Ruby，先要理解它为什么愿意为「人的表达力」付出运行时代价，又如何在近十年里用 JIT 和并发模型把这笔代价一点点赚回来。\n\n这个 hub 把 Ruby 拆成四条层层递进的主线，每一章都建立在前一章的地基之上。\n\n第一条主线是**基础**。我们从「一切皆对象」的世界观出发，看清 Ruby 的对象模型如何贯穿整门语言；再落到日常语法与惯用法，理解什么叫「写得像 Ruby 的 Ruby」；最后单独剖开块（block）这个 Ruby 最独特的语法构件，它是后面所有 DSL 与迭代器的源头。没有这一章，后面的元编程会显得像魔法。\n\n第二条主线是**对象系统**。Ruby 的面向对象不是 Java 式的静态契约，而是一套运行时可以被打开、被改写、被观察的活系统。类与模块给出组合的骨架，元编程给出在运行时生成代码的能力，方法查找与 `method_missing` 则揭示了「调用一个方法」背后那条可被拦截的祖先链。这三篇互为表里：元编程之所以可能，正是因为方法查找是动态的。\n\n第三条主线是**生态**。语言本身只是入口，真正让 Ruby 在 2026 年仍然活跃的是它的工程生态。Gem 与 Bundler 解决依赖与分发，Rails 把 Ruby 的表达力放大成全栈 Web 框架的生产力，而 Ractor 与 Fiber 则回答了那个困扰 Ruby 多年的问题：在全局锁之下如何做真正的并发与并行。\n\n第四条主线是**运行时**，它是整个 hub 的落地与收口。MRI 与 YJIT/ZJIT 讲清代码如何被执行与即时编译，垃圾回收与内存讲清对象在堆上的生与死，性能与剖析则教你用数据而非直觉去优化。前三章关心「怎么写」，这一章关心「写出来之后机器到底做了什么」。\n\n四章读完，你对 Ruby 的认识会从「一门好用的脚本语言」变成「一套可解释、可观测、可调优的完整运行时」。建议按顺序阅读，因为每一章都在为下一章铺设词汇与心智模型。\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/ruby-language/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"ruby-philosophy","title":"Ruby 哲学与对象模型","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/ruby-language/foundations/ruby-philosophy"},{"seq":2,"slug":"syntax-idioms","title":"语法与惯用法","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/ruby-language/foundations/syntax-idioms"},{"seq":3,"slug":"blocks-procs-lambdas","title":"块、Proc 与 Lambda","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/ruby-language/foundations/blocks-procs-lambdas"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"oop","title":"对象系统","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/ruby-language/oop","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"classes-modules","title":"类与模块","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/ruby-language/oop/classes-modules"},{"seq":2,"slug":"metaprogramming-ruby","title":"元编程","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/ruby-language/oop/metaprogramming-ruby"},{"seq":3,"slug":"method-dispatch","title":"方法查找与 method_missing","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/ruby-language/oop/method-dispatch"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"ecosystem","title":"生态","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/ruby-language/ecosystem","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"gems-bundler","title":"Gem 与 Bundler","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/ruby-language/ecosystem/gems-bundler"},{"seq":2,"slug":"rails-overview","title":"Rails 与 Web 开发","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/ruby-language/ecosystem/rails-overview"},{"seq":3,"slug":"concurrency-ruby","title":"并发：Ractor 与 Fiber","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/ruby-language/ecosystem/concurrency-ruby"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"runtime","title":"运行时","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/ruby-language/runtime","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"mri-yjit","title":"MRI 与 YJIT","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/ruby-language/runtime/mri-yjit"},{"seq":2,"slug":"gc-memory","title":"垃圾回收与内存","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/ruby-language/runtime/gc-memory"},{"seq":3,"slug":"performance-profiling","title":"性能与剖析","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/ruby-language/runtime/performance-profiling"}]}]}